    "sample_id": "helpsteer3:train:983507900bfeae21146547e21e32b96984bdc6a3595eaa2dd6ee6188c73b7190",
    "task": "(In the school literature clubroom…)\n\nMonika: “There we go! Everything’s all set up for today’s meeting.”\n\nSayori: “Thanks for getting everything ready, Monika! I’m excited to discuss the new book we’re reading.”\n\nNatsuki: “Yeah, me too. I’ve already got a bunch of notes and thoughts on it.”\n\nMonika: “I’m glad to see you two so enthusiastic. What about you, Yuri? …Yuri? Where is she?”\n\nSayori: “She’s actually at the hospital right now. She sent me a text yesterday, saying that she was going in for her 7-month",
    "chosen": " check-up.\"\n\nMonika: \"Oh, that's right! I remember her mentioning that. I hope everything goes well. We'll have to fill her in on our discussion later.\"\n\nNatsuki: \"Yeah, I hope she's okay. But for now, let's get started! What did everyone think of the book so far?\"\n\nSayori: \"I really liked it! The characters are so interesting, and the story is already getting so intense.\"\n\nMonika: \"I agree. The author's use of imagery is beautiful. It reminds me a bit of Yuri's writing style, actually.\"\n\nNatsuki: \"Yeah, speaking of that, I wanted to talk about the symbolism in the first chapter. I think there's a lot more going on than what's on the surface.\"\n\n(The three of them continue their discussion, taking notes and sharing their thoughts. Meanwhile, Sayori's phone buzzes with a message from Yuri.)\n\nSayori: \"Hold on, guys. It's Yuri. She says... 'Check-up went well. Doctor says everything is fine. Found out the baby's gender! It's a girl!'\"\n\nMonika: \"Aww, that's wonderful news! We should do something special for her when she gets back.\"\n\nNatsuki: \"Yeah, like a mini baby shower or something! We could get her some cute baby books to read.\"\n\nSayori: \"That's a great idea! Let's plan it for our next meeting. For now, let's keep discussing the book so we can fill her in later.\"\n\n(The three of them smile and continue their literature club meeting, looking forward to celebrating Yuri's good news with her soon.)",
    "rejected": "It seems like Yuri is currently at the hospital for her 7-month check-up. It's important for her to take care of her health and attend regular check-ups. The literature club meeting can continue without her, and the members can discuss the new book as planned. They can also share their thoughts and notes with Yuri once she returns from the hospital.",
